From c278b13de031cb6dc41c7aeaf05f089ea89e5755 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aryan Randeriya <aryan.k.randeriya@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 20:42:45 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 16/18] fix(render): scope :has() removal invalidation to the
 removed features

Every light-DOM removal re-cascaded the whole document on nytimes.com
(`planned_dirty=5470`, 2.4-3.5 s per geometry read after a removeChild).
The planner fired every `:has()` rule on every removal and walked all old
ancestors: NYT's `body:has(.k27EHG_expandedPromoFeed)` then anchored on
<body>, whose subtree is the document.

As Blink and WebKit do, a removal now fires a `:has()` only when the removed
subtree carried a feature (tag, class, id, attribute) of its argument, or
when the argument has a sibling/structural side effect on an element that
stays and that element carries a key. The runtime cannot rely on the
detached subtree at flush time (it may have been edited, or its old parent
removed or moved since), so `TreeStyleMutation::remove` records the
subtree's features and the old ancestor chain when the removal happens.

The walk to the anchors follows the argument's traversal scope: `> .x`
reaches only the old parent (and only a removed root that is `.x`), `+`/`~`
only the old parent's children, a descendant combinator every old ancestor;
mixed or nested combinators keep the old every-boundary walk. A `:has()`
inside `:is()`/`:where()`/`:not()` takes the anchor key of the compound
around it (GitHub's `.col:not(:has(+ .dummy))`), as do structural pseudos
there.

The runtime now builds retained-style records only for connected changes
to a prepared render, so detached DOM building does not pay for the
snapshot.

Removal read on a NYT snapshot: 3.5 s -> 0.3 s (planned_dirty 5088 -> 13);
live nytimes.com: 2.5 s -> 0.25 s. Retained results match a forced full
recalc on nytimes.com, YouTube, GitHub and Wikipedia after removals.

Tests: equivalence with a full cascade for removing a `:has()` argument or
its holder, a `body:has()` flag, an unkeyed-anchor child argument, text
under `:empty`; removals after the old parent is detached or moved and
after a detached edit; locality (<= 40 fresh of 2000+) for unrelated
removals and for child/sibling/`:not()` arguments.

